(:id "port/python/packet/floats" :state :done :evidence ("internal/codegen/python/python_packet_floats_test.go: TestPythonPacketFloats/contract" "internal/codegen/python/python_packet_floats_test.go: TestPythonPacketFloats/finite" "internal/codegen/python/python_packet_floats_test.go: TestPythonPacketFloats/goldens" "make packet-finite-python" "make packet-finite-python-negative-control (TestPythonPacketFloats/negative-control/finite-read, finite-write)") :tested-revision "7f14968f9657d4c79d53ff523d641854e706cb2a" :note "2026-11-15: TestPythonPacketFloats generated its fixture schemas and test/packet-finite/python into temp directories and ran them under the pinned CPython 3.15.2 and 3.11.18 with mypy --strict over every generated tree; packet-finite-python passed under both pins (86 vectors) and packet-finite-python-negative-control went red by name in each direction. Run on Linux x86_64 under SCHEMA_SLOW=1 at this revision. Raw float32 and float64 ride bit exact, NaN and infinity are refused on write as InvalidValue naming the field and on read by their raw bits as Refused, and a double that rounds past the largest float32 is refused; the rigidbody_at_rest and rigidbody_moving C++ pins read and write back byte-identical.")
(:id "port/python/packet/compressed-float" :state :done :evidence ("internal/codegen/python/python_packet_floats_test.go: TestPythonPacketFloats/contract" "internal/codegen/python/python_packet_floats_test.go: TestPythonPacketFloats/goldens/compressed_probe" "internal/codegen/python/python_packet_floats_test.go: TestPythonPacketFloats/negative-control/generated") :tested-revision "7f14968f9657d4c79d53ff523d641854e706cb2a" :note "2026-11-15: TestPythonPacketFloats generated its fixture schemas and test/packet-finite/python into temp directories and ran them under the pinned CPython 3.15.2 and 3.11.18 with mypy --strict over every generated tree; packet-finite-python passed under both pins (86 vectors) and packet-finite-python-negative-control went red by name in each direction. Run on Linux x86_64 under SCHEMA_SLOW=1 at this revision. The compressed float32 rides the runtime quantizer's step index, matches the wire laid out in Go from SPEC 4.3, refuses a value outside its declared range on write and a step in the bit headroom on read; the compressed_probe C++ pin reads and writes back byte-identical; the control cuts the generated range check and the probe names exactly its vectors.")
(:id "port/python/packet/fixed-point" :state :done :evidence ("internal/codegen/python/python_packet_floats_test.go: TestPythonPacketFloats/contract" "internal/codegen/python/python_packet_floats_test.go: TestPythonPacketFloats/negative-control/fixed-read" "internal/codegen/python/python_test.go: TestPythonRefusesUncarriedKindsByName") :tested-revision "7f14968f9657d4c79d53ff523d641854e706cb2a" :note "2026-11-15: TestPythonPacketFloats generated its fixture schemas and test/packet-finite/python into temp directories and ran them under the pinned CPython 3.15.2 and 3.11.18 with mypy --strict over every generated tree; packet-finite-python passed under both pins (86 vectors) and packet-finite-python-negative-control went red by name in each direction. Run on Linux x86_64 under SCHEMA_SLOW=1 at this revision. fixed(16, 16), ufixed(8, 8), a degenerate fixed(16, 16) and fixed(112, 16) ride the raw scaled integer's offset from min << F, match the wire laid out in Go from SPEC 4.3, refuse a raw value outside [min << F, max << F] or a non-int on write and an offset past the raw span on read. The C++ pins that use fixed point (ludicrous_state, ludicrous_state_untargeted, degenerate_probe) also need arrays or int128 and stay on the skip list for the close card.")
